Subject: Re: SDK setup & endpoint migration — next steps

Thanks Vanessa. Quick technical notes and a sample snippet for the team.

Engineer notes:
- Sandbox region: dev-us1 (non-prod) — traffic will be isolated.
- Token rotation: recommend short-lived keys (1 hr) for CI; production tokens 24 hr with refresh endpoint.
- KV cache: warm prefixes before cutover to avoid cold-start penalties on first heavy requests.

Node sample (minimal) — include in quickstart:

const fetch = require('node-fetch');
async function generate(prompt) {
  const res = await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json',
      'x-rw-auth': process.env.RW_KEY
    },
    body: JSON.stringify({ model: 'rw-medium', prompt }),
    // client-side timeout handled via AbortController in production
  });
  if (res.status === 429) throw new Error('rate_limited');
  return res.json();
}

Suggested timeout/retry pseudo: base_timeout=10000ms, attempts=4, backoff=exp(200ms)*jitter, max_backoff=5000ms. For batch inference, set per-batch timeout to 30s.

Cutover checklist (technical highlights)
- Pre-cutover: warm caches, run 1M token synthetic for latency profiling.
- 10% traffic: monitor per-route p50/p95, token cost.
- Rollback path: DNS swap back + token disable.

I'll own sandbox readiness. Jordan, can you share the allowlist IPs and the small healthcheck script?

— Vivek
